{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U10 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are both connected to net GND. U11 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are also both connected to net GND.",
      "expected": "The isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 should have their logic-side ground (GND1) and isolated-side ground (GND2) on separate nets to maintain galvanic isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The isolation barrier is bypassed, so the CAN buses are not galvanically isolated. This defeats the purpose of the isolated transceivers and can cause ground loops, noise, or damage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U1", "U2", "U15", "U18", "U19", "U22", "U27", "U29", "U30", "U34", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": [],
      "nets": [],
      "observed": "The value field for these buffers is \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\", but the MPN field is \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\" (a 1G125 tri-state buffer). The symbol includes an /OE pin, which the 1G07 open-drain buffer does not have.",
      "expected": "The specification calls for SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffers, particularly for U15, U22, U35, and U36 in the e-stop circuit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled with the MPN, the buffers are push-pull tri-state devices instead of open-drain. This can cause contention on the e-stop loop and changes the drive behavior from the intended open-drain sink.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R36 has value \"24k\", but its MPN is \"FRC0805J240TSD\" and its description states \"24Ω\". The part number decodes to 24Ω, not 24kΩ.",
      "expected": "R36 should be 24kΩ as indicated by its value field and its role as a bleeder resistor across the PoE output (VOUTP/VOUTN).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled using the MPN, a 24Ω resistor will be placed across the PoE output. At 48V this would dissipate about 96W, likely destroying the resistor and damaging the board.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: the isolated CAN transceivers have their isolated grounds shorted to logic ground, the e-stop buffers are specified as SN74LVC1G07 but sourced as 1G125 tri-state parts, and R36 has a value/MPN mismatch that would place a 24Ω resistor across the PoE output instead of 24kΩ."
}

